  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "And then: -고",
     "texto": [
      "To link related actions, add **-고** to the stem of the first verb: 보다 → **보고**, 먹다 → **먹고**. In a simple sequence with the same subject, it is usually enough to mark the past on the last verb: 바다를 **보고** 사진을 찍었어요 = I saw the sea and took photos.",
      "It is not an absolute rule: the past can also appear before -고 when the clauses are presented as separate facts or when their time relationship is emphasised."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "So, but, by the way",
     "texto": [
      "**그래서** = so, that's why. 날씨가 좋았어요. **그래서** 많이 걸었어요 (the weather was good; so I walked a lot).",
      "**하지만** = but.",
      "**그런데** = but, and also «by the way», to change the subject.",
      "**그리고** = and, also."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "For telling about a trip",
     "texto": [
      "**도착했어요** = I arrived. **탔어요** = I took (transport). **걸었어요** = I walked. **구경했어요** = I visited, I went sightseeing.",
      "**어땠어요?** = How was it? It is the past of 어때요. **좋았어요** = it was good.",
      "**다시** = again."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
